WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.310
<v Krista>In this video we're talking about</v>

2
00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.770
multiplication and division of mixed numbers.

3
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.950
Remember that a mixed number

4
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.100
is a whole number plus a fraction.

5
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.770
So when I say 4 1/2, I have the whole number four

6
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.743
and the fraction 1/2, and this is 4 1/2,

7
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.920
which is halfway between four and five.

8
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.520
So, we have mixed numbers.

9
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.080
What happens when we want to multiple mixed numbers,

10
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.170
or we want to divide mixed numbers?

11
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.830
Well, the easiest way to do it is going to be

12
00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.870
to change the mixed numbers into an improper fraction.

13
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.840
And the way that we do that is, we'll start here with 4 1/2.

14
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.070
We want to change this to an improper fraction.

15
00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.530
Remember that an improper fraction

16
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.420
is a fraction where the numerator

17
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.210
is greater than or equal to the denominator.

18
00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.970
So here, to change the mixed number into

19
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.050
an improper fraction, we're going to take the denominator,

20
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.230
which is two, multiply it by the whole number.

21
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.940
So two times four gives us eight.

22
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.400
Then, to that result I'm going to add the numerator.

23
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.660
So eight plus one is nine, and then I take

24
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.200
nine and put it over my original denominator.

25
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.980
So, 4 1/2 becomes 9/2, then I'm going to

26
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.810
multiple that by whatever I get

27
00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.900
when I change 5 3/4 to an improper fraction.

28
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.630
So I'll do four times five is 20, 20 plus three is 23.

29
00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:09.400
So then I take 23 over my original denominator, or 23/4.

30
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.500
And now, I've turned this just into a simple

31
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.100
fraction multiplication problem,

32
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.610
so I multiply across my numerators.

33
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:20.020
Nine times 23 gives me 207.

34
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.620
And two times four gives me 8.

35
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.010
I can't reduce this fraction at all,

36
00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.350
so this is my final answer.

37
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.150
I can leave my final answer as an improper fraction,

38
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.490
where the numerator is greater than

39
00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.950
or equal to the denominator.

40
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.180
Or, if I want to, I can change it back into a mixed number.

41
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.280
If I want to change it back into a mixed number,

42
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.700
I just divide eight into 207.

43
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.700
So I say, eight into 207, eight goes into 20 two times,

44
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.890
two times eight is 16, subtracting 16 from 20 I get 4,

45
00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.220
then I bring down the seven.

46
00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.790
Eight goes into 47 five times, five times eight is 40,

47
00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.790
and my remainder then is seven.

48
00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.360
So because seven is less than eight, my remainder here

49
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.670
is less than my divisor, I know that I'm done.

50
00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:07.490
And I can say that 207/8 is the same thing as 25 here,

51
00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.270
I take my result, 25,

52
00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.276
and then the remainder over the divisor.

53
00:02:11.276 --> 00:02:16.040
So 25 7/8 is the same thing as 207.

54
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.220
Let's do another example with multiplication.

55
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.653
Here I have 2 1/4 times 1 1/5.

56
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.990
I want to change them to improper fractions.

57
00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.300
So this first one here, I'm going to do

58
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.430
four times two is eight, eight plus one is nine.

59
00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.260
So I'm going to get nine over my original denominator of four.

60
00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.340
I'm multiplying that by 1 1/5,

61
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.640
so five times one gives me five,

62
00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.960
five plus one gives me six, so I'm going to have 6/5.

63
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.190
Then I just multiply across my numerators.

64
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:46.660
Nine times six is 54, four times five is 20.

65
00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.530
And remember, I can leave my final answer

66
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:50.330
as an improper fraction, but it has to be

67
00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.150
a reduced improper fraction, and I can reduce this fraction

68
00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.960
by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by two.

69
00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.620
So when I divide both by two, I'll get 27/10.

70
00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.930
And now this is a reduced improper fraction.

71
00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.900
I can leave it this way, or I can change it back

72
00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.970
to a mixed number by dividing 10 into 27.

73
00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.630
So I can do the long division, or I can just realize that

74
00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.910
10 will go into 27 two times, but not three times,

75
00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.500
because ten times three would be 30,

76
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.340
which would be greater than 27.

77
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.690
So I know it'll go in two times,

78
00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.713
and I'll just be left with 7/10.

79
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.380
So it's either 27/10, or 2 7/10.

80
00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.070
Either answer is acceptable.

81
00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.290
Now what happens when I want to divide mixed numbers?

82
00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.940
Here I have 4 1/2 divided by 5 3/4.

83
00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.030
Well, we want to start the same way we did before,

84
00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.830
